examples.solution_text:
Add the durations along each directed path from Start to Finish.

Path $A$–$C$:
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}3+5\\&=8\text{ days}\end{aligned}$

Path $A$–$B$–$D$–$E$:
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}3+4+2+7\\&=16\text{ days}\end{aligned}$

The longest path is $A$–$B$–$D$–$E$. The minimum completion time is $16$ days.

