\tikzset{midarrow/.style={decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\arrow{stealth}}},postaction={decorate}}}
\coordinate (S) at (0,0);\coordinate (P) at (2,1.3);\coordinate (Q) at (2,-1.3);\coordinate (R) at (4,0);\coordinate (Z) at (6,0);
\draw[midarrow] (S)--(P) node[midway,above left] {$A,\ 5$};
\draw[midarrow] (S)--(Q) node[midway,below left] {$B,\ 4$};
\draw[midarrow] (P)--(R) node[midway,above right] {$C,\ 7$};
\draw[midarrow] (Q)--(R) node[midway,below right] {$D,\ 3$};
\draw[midarrow] (R)--(Z) node[midway,above] {$E,\ 2$};
\foreach \v in {S,P,Q,R,Z}{\fill[black] (\v) circle (2pt);}
\node[left] at (S) {Start};\node[right] at (Z) {Finish};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
a. Find the float time of activity $D$.
b. Activity $D$ takes $2$ days longer than planned. Will the project finish later?
c. Instead, activity $C$ takes $1$ day longer than planned. Will the project finish later?

examples.solution_text:
a. A forward scan gives $5$ at the end of $A$ and $4$ at the end of $B$. At the merge, choose the larger value:
$\begin{aligned}t_R&=\max(5+7,4+3)\\&=12\end{aligned}$

The finish time is $12+2=14$ days. A backward scan gives $14-2=12$ at the merge.

The solution diagram shows earliest and latest event times as $(\mathrm{EST},\mathrm{LST})$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},>=stealth]
\usetikzlibrary{decorations.markings}
\tikzset{midarrow/.style={decoration={markings,mark=at position 0.5 with {\arrow{stealth}}},postaction={decorate}}}
\definecolor{scanblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\coordinate (S) at (0,0);\coordinate (P) at (2,1.3);\coordinate (Q) at (2,-1.3);\coordinate (R) at (4,0);\coordinate (Z) at (6,0);
\draw[midarrow] (S)--(P) node[midway,above left] {$A,\ 5$};
\draw[midarrow] (S)--(Q) node[midway,below left] {$B,\ 4$};
\draw[midarrow] (P)--(R) node[midway,above right] {$C,\ 7$};
\draw[midarrow] (Q)--(R) node[midway,below right] {$D,\ 3$};
\draw[midarrow] (R)--(Z) node[midway,above] {$E,\ 2$};
\foreach \v in {S,P,Q,R,Z}{\fill[black] (\v) circle (2pt);}
\node[left] at (S) {Start};\node[right] at (Z) {Finish};
\node[below,text=scanblue] at (S) {$(0,0)$};
\node[above,text=scanblue] at (P) {$(5,5)$};
\node[below,text=scanblue] at (Q) {$(4,9)$};
\node[above,text=scanblue] at (R) {$(12,12)$};
\node[below,text=scanblue] at (Z) {$(14,14)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Use the latest time at the destination, subtract the duration and the earliest time at the starting vertex:
$\begin{aligned}\text{Float of }D&=12-3-4\\&=5\text{ days}\end{aligned}$

b. The $2$-day increase uses less than $D$'s $5$ days of float. The project still finishes in $14$ days.

c. The critical path is $A$–$C$–$E$, so $C$ has zero float. Its $1$-day increase delays the project by $1$ day, giving $15$ days.

