Find $x$ and identify the critical path.

examples.solution_text:
Compare the paths whose durations are known.

Path $B$: $9$ hours.

Path $C$–$D$:
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}4+3\\&=7\text{ hours}\end{aligned}$

Path $C$–$E$–$G$:
$\begin{aligned}&\mathrel{\phantom{=}}4+2+6\\&=12\text{ hours}\end{aligned}$

These are all shorter than $19$ hours, so $A$–$F$ must be the critical path.
$\begin{aligned}5+x&=19\\x&=14\end{aligned}$

Activity $F$ takes $14$ hours. The critical path is $A$–$F$.

The solution diagram marks the critical path and fills in the unknown duration.
